# Mosh landing page — waitlist config TEMPLATE (safe to commit; no real values here).
# Copy to .env.local for local dev (gitignored); set the same names in your host's
# dashboard (Vercel / Cloudflare Pages) for production. These are PUBLIC_-prefixed on
# purpose: this is a static site with no server, so they're read at BUILD time and
# baked into the shipped JS bundle — anyone can read them in devtools. That's expected
# and safe for an anon/publishable key (see supabase/README.md's "safe to embed/share"
# table); never put a service_role key or anything secret behind a PUBLIC_ name.
#
# Default target: the form POSTs directly to Supabase's PostgREST API using the anon
# key, inserting a row into the `waitlist` table created by
# supabase/migrations/<ts>_waitlist.sql (RLS is insert-only — the anon key can add a
# row but can never read the list back).

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional override: if set, the form POSTs JSON { email, source } here instead of
# talking to Supabase directly (e.g. a custom Edge Function, a webhook, a different
# backend entirely). Contract: respond 2xx for a new signup, 409 for an address
# that's already on the list, anything else is treated as an error.
PUBLIC_WAITLIST_URL=

# Optional: a short label stored in the `source` column. Defaults to "landing".
# Useful if a second landing page/campaign ever exists and you want to tell
# signups apart.
PUBLIC_WAITLIST_SOURCE=
